-- The late fee of 2 a day from `37-days-between-dates-refused.velle`, written the one way that
-- validates: every night a loan that is out and past due gets one LateDay record, and the fee is
-- 2 times the number of them. `velle validate` prints "`38-days-between-dates-workaround.velle`
-- validates."
--
-- It gives up the meaning. The fee counts the nights the Nightly schedule ran while the loan was
-- late, not the days between `dueOn` and `returnedOn`, so a night whose run is missed may be a day
-- the member is not charged for (whether a missed run is made up is open, OQ34). It also keeps a
-- record per late day that the business never asked for.
act Loan {
    dueOn: Date
    returnedOn: Date?
    lateFee: decimal = 2 * count(lateDays)
}

shape LateDay {
    loan: one Loan
    countedOn: Date
}

rule CountLateDay
    when (Loan where returnedOn is none and dueOn < today and not exists (LateDay where loan == this and countedOn == today))
    on Nightly {
    LateDay from { loan: this, countedOn: today }
}
